 qualify:["Income is documented like agency full doc: two years W-2s/tax returns, paystubs, and 4506-C transcripts","Self-employed borrowers need two years of personal and business returns with stable or rising trend","Reserves are verified from seasoned, sourced liquid and retirement assets; retirement is often discounted","Appraisal is reviewed hard for comparable support at the price point; a desk review or second appraisal may be ordered"],
 docs:["Two years W-2s and/or full tax returns","30 days of paystubs","Two to three months of complete bank and investment statements","Retirement statements for reserves","Purchase contract or current mortgage statement","Explanation letters for large deposits and credit inquiries"],
 pros:["Finances high-value homes in a single loan without a piggyback second","No mortgage insurance on most programs","Competitive pricing for strong borrowers because the credit risk is low","Fixed and ARM structures available"],
 cons:["Tighter credit, reserve and DTI standards than conforming","Larger down payment and cash-to-close","Appraisal scrutiny can delay or derail purchases","Guidelines and appetite shift with investor capital markets"],
 pitfalls:["Under-documenting large deposits or gift funds late in the process","Assuming the county is at baseline when it is a high-cost county (or vice versa) and quoting the wrong product","Letting the borrower open new credit or move money between accounts before closing","Not counting reserves required for all other financed properties"],
 find:["Listing agents in luxury and move-up neighborhoods","Financial planners and wealth managers whose clients are buying or relocating","Corporate relocation and HR contacts","Open houses and broker caravans for higher-priced listings","Your own past-client database for equity growth past conforming"],
